FEX on Android: a SIGSEGV on FEX's own PROT_NONE pages counts as theirs with SEGV_MAPERR as well
as SEGV_ACCERR.

FEX takes a fault on the thread's InterruptFaultPage (which delivers deferred signals) and on the
JIT guard page as its own only with si_code SEGV_ACCERR. Kernels with speculative page faults
report a write to a populated PROT_NONE page of a multithreaded process as SEGV_MAPERR, and such a
fault then reached the guest as a real SIGSEGV. Both checks now take either code; the faulting
address alone tells whether the page is FEX's.

