+// A kernel fault on one of FEX's own PROT_NONE pages (the JIT guard page, the InterruptFaultPage).
+// Kernels with speculative page faults report a write to a populated PROT_NONE page of a
+// multithreaded process as SEGV_MAPERR rather than SEGV_ACCERR, so both count; the faulting address
+// decides whether the page is FEX's. Signals sent by a process (tgkill, sigqueue) have other codes.
+static bool IsKernelProtectionFault(const siginfo_t& SigInfo) {
+  return SigInfo.si_code == SEGV_ACCERR || SigInfo.si_code == SEGV_MAPERR;
+}
